Scaling Prometheus with Federation
Objectives
Design and operate a hierarchical Prometheus federation topology in which a global aggregator scrapes selected metrics from two independent cluster-level Prometheus instances
Author PromQL recording rules and alerting rules on the global instance that aggregate cross-cluster signals into unified time series
Diagnose label collision, cardinality, and scrape-lag problems that arise specifically in federated architectures
Prerequisites
Comfort with Linux process management, systemd unit files, and reading structured log output
Familiarity with YAML syntax and HTTP-based APIs (curl, status codes, response bodies)
Prior exposure to basic PromQL concepts: selectors, rate(), sum(), and label matchers
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

