Task 2: Implement the Federation Topology and Validate Cross-Cluster Metrics
Step 2.1 â Confirm the /federate endpoint delivers labelled time series
The /federate endpoint (a Prometheus-native HTTP endpoint that returns metrics in the Prometheus text exposition format) is the mechanism by which the global instance pulls a filtered subset of time series from each cluster instance. Before writing any rules, verify that the endpoint on each cluster instance returns time series that carry the cluster and region labels injected by external_labels.

Your verification must satisfy all three of the following conditions:

A raw HTTP request to http://localhost:9090/federate with a match[] parameter returns at least the up metric with a cluster="cluster-a" label present on every returned line.
The same check against port 9091 returns cluster="cluster-b" on every returned line.
A query against the global instance at port 9092 for the metric up returns results whose cluster label distinguishes the two source clusters, confirming that honor_labels: true preserved the originating labels rather than overwriting them with the federation job's own labels.
