Step 3.2 â Validate end-to-end aggregation and cardinality constraints
With application metrics flowing through the full federation pipeline, verify the following four conditions against the global instance at port 9092. Each condition must be confirmed by a direct API query, not by visual inspection of the web UI.

Condition 1 â Cross-cluster request rate: A PromQL query computing sum by (cluster) (rate(app_http_requests_total[2m])) against the global instance returns two result vectors, one per cluster, each with a non-zero value.

Condition 2 â Latency percentile: A PromQL query computing the 95th-percentile request duration per cluster using histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (cluster, le) (rate(app_request_duration_seconds_bucket[2m]))) returns two result vectors with values within the histogram's defined bucket range.

Condition 3 â Label preservation: Every result vector returned by the global instance for app_http_requests_total carries a cluster label whose value is either cluster-a or cluster-b, confirming that honor_labels: true and external_labels on the cluster instances are working correctly together.

Condition 4 â Cardinality budget: The total number of active time series on the global instance, reported by prometheus_tsdb_head_series scraped from port 9092, must remain below 2000. If it exceeds this threshold, tighten the match[] selectors in the federation configuration to drop high-cardinality series that are not needed at the global level.

