Conclusion
This lab demonstrated how Prometheus federation creates a two-tier monitoring architecture in which cluster-level instances own their own scrape cycles and the global instance selectively pulls only the metrics required for cross-cluster visibility. The honor_labels directive and external_labels block work together to ensure that label provenance is preserved through the federation boundary without collision. Keeping the match[] selectors narrow is the primary operational lever for controlling cardinality growth on the global instance as the number of federated clusters scales.
